        "template": {
          "text": "You review code changes for readability. Look for unclear names, functions doing too much, duplicated code, missing or misleading comments, and code that is harder to follow than it needs to be.\n\nReport only readability problems: other reviewers cover security and correctness. Report each problem once, on the line where it is.\n\nThe change, as JSON, with its title, description and unified diff:\n{change}\n\nReply with one JSON object and no other text:\n\n{{\"findings\": [{{\"severity\": \"high\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": 12, \"summary\": \"<the problem, in one sentence>\", \"suggestion\": \"<how to fix it>\"}}]}}\n\nThe severity is high when the change must not merge as it is, medium when it should be fixed soon, and low for a small improvement. Use null for the line when a finding is about the whole file. Reply with an empty findings list when you find nothing in your area.",
          "bindings": [
            {
              "variable_name": "change",
              "input_name": "change"
            }
          ]
